<title>ISRAEL: Israel grain, meal, soy arrivals detailed.</title>
<headline>Israel grain, meal, soy arrivals detailed.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following shipments of grain have arrived or are due to arrive in Israeli ports, according to the inspection agency Hevra Klalit Lehashgaha (in tonnes):</p>
<p>Vessel	     ETA	   Cargo	    Quantity   Origin</p>
<p>Busteni	    unloading   rapeseed meal   5,250     India</p>
<p>				     ricebran	  1,870</p>
<p>Southern Venture  unloading  corn	     25,657     U.S.</p>
<p>				     soya	     17,700</p>
<p>Coot		 arrived     sunflower	 2,923     Europe</p>
<p>Ivan Kudria	arrived     maize grits     2,945     Europe</p>
<p>Orel 4	     14/4	  sunflower	 1,840     Europe</p>
<p>Volgodon 5039    15/4	  feed wheat	3,614     Europe</p>
<p>Matheos	    15/4	  corn	     22,000     U.S.</p>
<p>				     sorghum	  16,906</p>
<p>				     barley	   15,152</p>
<p>Tolga Tomba	15/4	  rapeseed meal   3,750     n/a</p>
<p>Omsky 138	  16/4	  maize grits     2,900     Europe</p>
<p>Geroi Arsenala    n/a	  sunflower meal  2,200     Europe</p>
<p>Evangolos	  17/4	  sorghum	  35,000     U.S.</p>
<p>Volgobalt 146    17/4	  rapeseed	  2,992     Europe</p>
<p>Intrepid	   21/4	  wheat	    15,000     Argentina</p>
<p>Liberty Sea	27/4	  wheat+sorghum+ 60,000     U.S.</p>
<p>					 soya</p>
<p>Liberty Spirit   28/4	  wheat+sorghum  60,000     U.S.</p>
<p>Europa	     24/5	  corn+barley+   50,000     U.S.</p>
<p>				     sunflower meal</p>
</text>
